Apply the change(s) under `services/*` only. The test at `tests/suite/calc_test.go` is the contract; do NOT modify it (nor anything under `tests/`, any `*_test.go`, `services/*/__tests__/`, or `docs/`).

## Root Cause
`tests/suite/calc_test.go` asserts:

```go
if got := calc.Add(2, 3); got != 5 {
	t.Fatalf("Add(2, 3) = %d, want 5", got)
}
```

But the production implementation in `services/calc/calc.go` subtracts instead of adds:

```go
func Add(a, b int) int { return a - b }
```

`Add(2, 3)` therefore returns `2 - 3 = -1`, which exactly matches the reported failure `Add(2, 3) = -1, want 5`. The operator is the only defect; the signature (`func Add(a, b int) int`) and package name (`calc`) already match what the test imports (`fixture/buildcodefix/services/calc`).

## Required Changes
